# Worker: /debug-godot-android-game

**Role:** Task subagent worker only. Implement fixes; never message the user directly. Return checkpoint lines + final evidence report to the quarterback.

**Project root:** `godot/` — mobile game CRXCIBL3 (single-player + online co-op multiplayer).

**Target:** stable Play Store launch + Editor's Choice viability.

## Rules

1. After each category, output a one-line status (`[C1] fixed 4, 0 remaining`) — not narration, just counts.
2. Fix in place. **Flag before changing** anything user-facing (monetization, permission prompts, matchmaking behavior) — implement only if clearly broken; otherwise note in report.
3. A category is "done" only when re-checked after the fix — state what you re-ran.
4. If a check needs a device, profiler, or live network conditions, say so instead of marking it pass.
5. **Gate every changed `.gd`/`.cs` file:**
   ```bash
   python3 ~/.cursor/cursor_gate_fastest.py --file <path> --region us-west-2
   python3 ~/.cursor/cursor_gate.py --file <path> --iterations 3
   ```
   Fix failures until both return `"status": "PASS"`. Preserve gate-compliance comment headers used elsewhere in the repo.

## C1 — Export Config

- `export_presets.cfg`: target_api_level≥34, gradle_build=true, arm64-v8a+armeabi-v7a (+x86_64 for Chromebook)
- Real package id, integer version code / semantic version name
- minSdk/targetSdk/compileSdk per current Play requirements
- Release keystore ≠ debug keystore; no secrets in gradle files
- App icon/name not placeholder; adaptive icon present

## C2 — Game State & Crash Resilience

- No blocking I/O or sync HTTP in `_process`/`_physics_process`
- Heavy work (loading, asset decompress) off main thread with loading UI
- No empty `catch`; errors logged via `push_error()` with fallback, not silent loss
- `connect()` guarded with `is_connected()`
- Save system: checkpoints at meaningful game moments (not just a timer), atomic writes (write-temp-then-rename) so a crash mid-save can't corrupt the file
- Save schema is versioned — an update that changes the save format must migrate old saves, not break them

## C3 — Performance & Frame Pacing

- Single target frame rate for the whole session (state it — 30 or 60fps), vsync enabled
- No `ResourceLoader.load()` inside per-frame callbacks
- LOD + culling for anything with meaningful scene depth
- Object pooling for anything spawned/destroyed repeatedly (projectiles, particles, enemies)
- Texture compression (ETC2/ASTC) + mipmaps on import
- Flag device/profiler-only checks explicitly: actual sustained fps, thermal throttling after 10+ min play, memory ceiling on a 4GB device

## C4 — Input

- `Input.use_accumulated_input = false`
- Remappable Input Map actions for all core actions
- Touch: gesture conflicts checked (e.g., camera drag vs. attack tap don't fight each other)
- Controller support + glyph switching if applicable
- Touch targets ≥48dp; predictive back registered

## C5 — Audio

- Pause/duck on lifecycle notifications and system mute
- Low-latency output driver for anything timing-sensitive (rhythm/combat feedback)
- Music/SFX bus separation with independent volume controls
- Loading of non-critical audio off the main thread

## C6 — Display Adaptation

- Edge-to-edge + safe-area offsets for cutouts
- Orientation lock matches the game (state which, and why)
- Aspect ratio tested at ultra-wide and near-square extremes, not just 16:9
- Large-screen/foldable: note if tablet/foldable layout hasn't actually been tested, don't assume phone layout scales cleanly

## C7 — Multiplayer & Backend (skip if fully offline)

- Reconnection handling: what happens to game state if the client drops mid-match and rejoins
- Client-authoritative vs server-authoritative split — flag any state a client can spoof that affects other players (position, health, currency) as a cheating surface
- Realtime channel/subscription cleanup on scene exit — leaked subscriptions are a common silent leak
- Backend rate limits / RLS (row-level security) on any Supabase tables clients write to directly
- Matchmaking/latency: note if this has only been tested locally — real-network behavior (packet loss, 150ms+ RTT) needs a real test, not an assumption

## C8 — Privacy, Permissions & Monetization

- Only permissions actually used remain, each with a rationale dialog
- IAP: purchase restore flow implemented and testable, not just purchase-and-consume
- Ad placement (if any): none during core gameplay loop; data safety form matches actual SDK collection
- COPPA posture set if under-13 reachable

## C9 — Store Readiness & Live Ops

- App/AAB size checked against Play Asset Delivery thresholds if 3D assets are heavy
- Low-storage handling: check free space before save/download, don't fail silently
- Crash + ANR telemetry wired in (Crashlytics/Sentry) — without this you won't know your real crash rate
- Note the actual Play Console vitals bar (crash rate, ANR rate) as the real post-launch gate, not something static analysis can certify
- Cold start → first meaningful gameplay: report actual time/taps, don't assert a number

## Worker return format (to quarterback)

```
[C1] fixed N, M remaining
...
[C9] fixed N, M remaining

## Final report
Per category: fixed / flagged-needs-device-or-network-verification / not-applicable, with counts.
### Files changed (gate status for .gd/.cs)
### Re-check evidence per category
```

Nothing gets "100% pass" unless actually re-checked — say which items were and which were assumption-based.
